    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n22170" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ĭn-ambŭlo</span></b> ,
			āre, v. n., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to walk up and down</i>, <i>pace to and fro</i> (class.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">paululum in porticu,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Rep. 1, 2</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">in viridi opacaque ripa,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Leg. 1, 5, 15</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">domi,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Att. 6, 2, 5</span></i>
			: cum quidam pransus ... manibus ad tergum rejectis
			inambularet, Asin. ap. <i><span class="en">Cic. Fam. 10, 32, 3</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">per muros,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					23, 43, 8</span></i>
			.— <i>Impers.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">inambulandumst,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. As. 3, 3, 92</span></i>
			.</div>
